    "versionNumber": 1,
    "name": "deadline-math-direct",
    "description": "Convert a published contest deadline to the reader's local time. Cases: day rollover, the weeks when the EU and US change clocks on different dates, 12 AM and AoE wording, non-hour offsets. Ground truth computed with zoneinfo.",
    "definition": "@kbench.task(\n    name=\"deadline-math-direct\",\n    # Literal y de 255 caracteres como m\u00c3\u00a1ximo: Kaggle rechaza la task si no.\n    description=(\n        \"Convert a published contest deadline to the reader's local time. Cases: day rollover, the weeks when \"\n        \"the EU and US change clocks on different dates, 12 AM and AoE wording, non-hour offsets. Ground truth \"\n        \"computed with zoneinfo.\"\n    ),\n)\ndef deadline_math(llm) -> float:\n    passed = 0\n    for case in CASE_SETS[SET]:\n        response = ask(llm, case)\n        answer = parse_answer(response)\n        kbench.assertions.assert_equal(\n            case.expected, answer,\n            expectation=f\"[{case.category}] {case.id}: {case.statement} -> {case.reader} = {case.expected}\",\n        )\n        passed += answer == case.expected\n    # Proporci\u00c3\u00b3n de aciertos: Kaggle a\u00c3\u00ban no muestra \u00c2\u00abaciertos de total\u00c2\u00bb (lee la tupla como valor \u00c2\u00b1 intervalo).\n    return passed / len(CASE_SETS[SET])\n"
  },
